WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.777
Window functions are powerful because they preserve row detail.

00:00:03.777 --> 00:00:08.257
GROUP BY usually reduces multiple rows to one grouped row.

00:00:08.257 --> 00:00:13.462
A window function can calculate a group average, rank, running total,

00:00:13.462 --> 00:00:17.257
or previous value while still returning the individual row.

00:00:17.257 --> 00:00:22.672
This is why windows are ideal when you need both detail and context in the same result.

00:00:22.672 --> 00:00:28.207
Window functions preserve detail rows while calculating across a related set.

00:00:28.207 --> 00:00:33.412
PARTITION BY defines independent groups, ORDER BY defines sequence,

00:00:33.412 --> 00:00:37.152
and the frame defines which neighboring rows participate.

00:00:37.152 --> 00:00:41.360
Those three choices are part of the business rule, not just syntax.
